:{"key":"27a0de2febb6b1f83479b6f67a54238c4dae003b","name":"Button","description":"Usage\nLarge is a default size of the button. The small size can be used in some specific cases when the large one is too big.\nThe button width depends on its label.\nThe button can't lead to another page — use the link instead.\nTruncate button's label if it doesn’t fit. Button label should never wrap. Avoid such long labels and translations. Truncating is a way to handle exception cases, but in the end the copy has to be updated.\n\n\nLoading\nThe button can be in the loading state: the button text is hidden and a spinner is shown in its place. Maintain the width that it would have if the text were visible. For examples, see the Styleguide.\n\n\nRow of actions\nThe distance between actions is defined in the variable actions-gap.\nThe behaviour of a row of actions is handled by the ButtonGroup component. We don't have any analogue in Figma, for designers it is simple row inside an Auto Layout. Feel free to the refer to the ButtonGroup component in communication with developers.","remote":true}},"schemaVersion":0,"styles":{}},"5512:7945":{"document":{"id":"5512:7945","name":"Control","type":"FRAME","scrollBehavior":"SCROLLS","componentPropertyReferences":{"visible":"Items per page#4923:10"},"children":[],"blendMode":"PASS_THROUGH","clipsContent":false,"background":[],"fills":[],"strokes":[],"strokeWeight":1.0,"strokeAlign":"INSIDE","backgroundColor":{"r":0.0,"g":0.0,"b":0.0,"a":0.0},"layoutMode":"HORIZONTAL","counterAxisAlignItems":"CENTER","itemSpacing":16.0,"layoutWrap":"NO_WRAP","absoluteBoundingBox":{"x":503.0,"y":1667.0,"width":177.0,"height":40.0},"absoluteRenderBounds":{"x":503.0,"y":1667.0,"width":177.0,"height":40.0},"constraints":{"vertical":"TOP","horizontal":"LEFT"},"layoutAlign":"INHERIT","layoutGrow":0.0,"layoutSizingHorizontal":"HUG","layoutSizingVertical":"HUG","effects":[],"interactions":[],"complexStrokeProperties":{"strokeType":"BASIC"}},"components":{},"componentSe